<odoo>
    <template id="show_website_info"
        inherit_id="website.show_website_info">
        <xpath
	        expr="//h1/small" position="replace">
	        <small>Viindoo Version <t t-out="version.get('server_version')"/></small>
        </xpath>
        <xpath expr="//p" position="replace">
            <p>Information about the <a target="_blank" href="https://about.viindoo.com">Viindoo Technology JSC.</a></p>
        </xpath>
        <!-- Chart of account and l10n app -->
        <xpath expr="//div[@t-if='l10n']/dl/dt/a" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="t-attf-href">https://viindoo.com/intro/accounting</attribute>
        </xpath>
    </template>
    
    <template id="layout" name="Main layout" inherit_id="website.layout">
		<xpath expr="//meta[@name='generator']" position="attributes">
			<attribute name="content">Viindoo</attribute>
		</xpath>

        <!-- The x_icon override that used to sit here is deliberately gone.
             It read:
                 <xpath expr="//t[@t-set='x_icon']" position="replace">
                     <t t-set="x_icon" t-value="'/viin_brand/static/img/favicon.ico'"/>
                 </xpath>
             locate_node (odoo/tools/template_inheritance.py) resolves an xpath to the FIRST
             document-order match, which in the combined website.layout arch is website's own
             producer (website/views/website_templates.xml:103,
             t-set x_icon = website.image_url(website, 'favicon')). Replacing it destroyed the
             website's configured favicon and substituted an unconditional brand path with no
             `or` guard, so a website that had configured its own favicon never got to serve it.
             Re-adding a guard would not help: after the replace, x_icon is unset at that point,
             so `x_icon or <brand>` still collapses to the brand every time.
             This block exists only on 18.0 - 17.0 has no such override - so removing it restores
             the 17.0 behaviour the forward-ported test in tests/test_website_title_not_preempted.py
             encodes. Non-website pages still get the brand default from viin_brand_common's own
             fallback in views/webclient_template.xml. -->
    </template>
</odoo>
